{
  "_comment": [
    "Real output of devalue@6.0.2 stringify(). Captured by running the package,",
    "not by reading its source, so the Nuxt decoder's tag test is pinned to the",
    "actual encoding rather than to an assumption about it.",
    "Regenerate with the probe in the devalue section of tests/README or by",
    "running: node -e \"const d=require('devalue'); ...\"",
    "The invariant decodeNuxtFlat depends on: an array node is either a list of",
    "numeric indexes (a plain array) or a list whose slot 0 is a type tag string.",
    "A plain array can never lead with a string, which is why the decoder treats",
    "a string in slot 0 as a tag."
  ],
  "devalueVersion": "6.0.2",
  "cases": [
    { "label": "strings first", "input": ["apple", "banana"], "flat": [[1, 2], "apple", "banana"] },
    { "label": "string then numbers", "input": ["apple", 42, true, null], "flat": [[1, 2, 3, 4], "apple", 42, true, null] },
    { "label": "string then nested", "input": ["apple", { "a": 1 }, [2, 3]], "flat": [[1, 2, 4], "apple", { "a": 3 }, 1, [5, 6], 2, 3] },
    { "label": "single string", "input": ["only"], "flat": [[1], "only"] },
    { "label": "numbers only", "input": [1, 2, 3], "flat": [[1, 2, 3], 1, 2, 3] },
    { "label": "object first", "input": [{ "a": 1 }, 2], "flat": [[1, 3], { "a": 2 }, 1, 2] },
    { "label": "null first", "input": [null, 1], "flat": [[1, 2], null, 1] },
    { "label": "bool first", "input": [true, false], "flat": [[1, 2], true, false] },
    { "label": "nested string array", "input": [["a", "b"], "c"], "flat": [[1, 4], [2, 3], "a", "b", "c"] },
    { "label": "deep in object", "input": { "data": { "books": ["x", "y"] } }, "flat": [{ "data": 1 }, { "books": 2 }, [3, 4], "x", "y"] },
    { "label": "tagged reactive", "input": { "a": 1 }, "flat": [{ "a": 1 }] }
  ]
}
